# Nexus private deployment
The authoritative repositories live on **test-host**, reached from Fedora with `ssh nexus-test`:
- `/etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra`: reusable public modules.
- `/etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra-Private`: concrete deployment and this runbook.
Dependency direction is private -> public. There are no Git remotes yet. The temporary local Git input is commit-pinned in `flake.lock`; commit public changes before running `nix flake update nexus-infra` in this repository. All components use the same pinned NixOS 26.05 package set.
## Deployment
| VM | Address | vCPUs | RAM | Service |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| test-vm | 10.80.0.2 | 1 | 256 MiB | Test HTTP on 8080 |
| network-control | 10.80.0.3 | 1 | 512 MiB | Headscale on 8080 |
| ingress | 10.80.0.4 | 1 | 256 MiB | Traefik on 80 |
All use QEMU/KVM, autostart, a read-only Nix-store share, and key-only SSH for `jonas`. AMD SVM must stay enabled in firmware. Guest SSH host keys persist in `vm-state`. The guest user has journal access but no passwordless sudo; on network-control, membership in the `headscale` group permits administration via its local Unix socket. The workstation public key is declared; private keys and account passwords are not in Git.
`hosts/test-host/` describes the machine/backend; `vms/` describes concrete instances; `cluster/test-host.nix` maps them to storage and addresses. `vms/common.nix` contains deployment access policy and the runtime persistence check.
## Storage
The Kingston system disk is unchanged: `/dev/sda1` is EFI, `/dev/sda2` is root. The Crucial CT500MX500SSD1, serial 1840E1D099EF, contains one 465.8 GiB ext4 partition labelled `nexus-data`, UUID `9f013958-f0b2-48cd-a1d4-3da7c4a067ac`, mounted by stable disk ID at `/srv/nexus-storage`.
The disk was already repurposed in the previous pass. This pass preserved all Nexus data, verified the former Debian root/swap offsets have no detectable filesystem signatures, and removed the two obsolete Debian EFI entries. No formatting/repartitioning occurred in this pass. Rebuilds never format disks.
A VM requests `nexus.persistence.<name>.mountPoint`; the private cluster supplies its `source` under the host-specific storage root. The public module generates virtiofs shares and orders startup after the backing mount and directory preparation. The guest never names a physical disk.
| VM | Name | Guest mount | Directory relative to host storage root |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| test-vm | test-data | /data | test-vm/test-data |
| network-control | control-state | /var/lib/headscale | network-control/control-state |
| ingress | ingress-state | /var/lib/traefik | ingress/ingress-state |
| each VM | vm-state | /var/lib/nexus | VM-name/vm-state |
Headscale's SQLite database and generated Noise key live only in persistent runtime storage. Future Traefik state belongs in its persistent directory; no TLS certificates are configured. Each share has a non-secret `.nexus-persistence-proof` marker written from inside its VM. Readable copies in `/run/nexus-proof/` support validation without exposing runtime secrets. The original `/data/persistence-proof.txt` remains unchanged.
## Network and ingress
`br-nexus` provides the private `10.80.0.0/24` L2 network; the host is `10.80.0.1`. Each VM has its own TAP. Physical Ethernet `enp27s0` remains on DHCP and is not attached to this bridge. This is a single-host foundation, not a cross-host overlay or migration implementation.
Only network-control has a default route and outbound NAT, scoped to `10.80.0.3/32`; it uses the existing LAN resolver. Headscale fetches its standard upstream Tailscale DERP directory. Embedded DERP, MagicDNS, client DNS overrides, OIDC and public TLS are disabled. Headscale is running locally, but no Tailscale clients are enrolled. It coordinates eventual peers; ordinary VM traffic crosses the bridge directly. Future clients should use direct peer-to-peer paths when possible, with a relay policy chosen later.
The only new LAN entry point is **http://192.168.178.192:8080/**:
```text
Fedora -> host LAN TCP socket :8080 -> ingress 10.80.0.4:80 (Traefik)
       -> test-vm 10.80.0.2:8080
```
The host's `systemd-socket-proxyd` transports TCP; Traefik performs HTTP routing. The listener binds only the host's LAN IPv4 address; it is not bound to the public IPv6 address. No public DNS, Cloudflare, public port forwarding, ACME or production TLS is configured. Traefik's dashboard is not enabled. This TCP transport does not preserve the original client IP in Traefik logs; it is deliberately a local test entry point.
## Commands from Fedora
Build/switch everything:
```sh
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo nixos-rebuild build --flake /etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra-Private#test-host'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake /etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra-Private#test-host'
```
Inspect all VMs and the LAN listener:
```sh
ssh nexus-test 'systemctl --no-pager --full status microvm@test-vm microvm@network-control microvm@ingress nexus-ingress.socket'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo journalctl -u microvm@test-vm -u microvm@network-control -u microvm@ingress -n 100 --no-pager'
```
Restart components (use `start` or `stop` in the same commands as needed):
```sh
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo systemctl restart microvm@test-vm.service'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo systemctl restart microvm@network-control.service'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo systemctl restart microvm@ingress.service'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo systemctl restart nexus-ingress.service'
```
Guest inspection uses temporary agent forwarding; the workstation key must be loaded in your SSH agent:
```sh
ssh -A nexus-test 'ssh jonas@10.80.0.2 "systemctl --no-pager status test-http"'
ssh -A nexus-test 'ssh jonas@10.80.0.3 "systemctl --no-pager status headscale; headscale users list"'
ssh -A nexus-test 'ssh jonas@10.80.0.4 "systemctl --no-pager status traefik; journalctl -u traefik -n 10 --no-pager"'
```
Test traffic, storage and boot entries:
```sh
curl -fsS http://192.168.178.192:8080/
ssh nexus-test 'curl -fsS http://10.80.0.3:8080/health'
ssh nexus-test 'curl -fsS http://10.80.0.2:8080/persistence-proof.txt'
ssh nexus-test 'lsblk -o NAME,SIZE,MODEL,FSTYPE,MOUNTPOINTS; findmnt /srv/nexus-storage'
ssh -t nexus-test 'sudo wipefs --no-act /dev/sdb /dev/sdb1; sudo efibootmgr'
```
Repeat the integration and restart/persistence checks (briefly interrupts the three VMs):
```sh
ssh -At nexus-test 'bash /etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra-Private/scripts/verify.sh --restart'
```
Omit `--restart` for service/connectivity checks. The script also ensures a harmless `nexus-persistence-check` Headscale user exists, to validate database persistence; it creates no auth keys or tokens. Evidence files contain only test markers, boot IDs, public host keys and this test user record. Sudo prompts normally; no password is stored in the script.
## Remaining work
- Reserve `192.168.178.192` in LAN DHCP, or deliberately update the listener address if it changes.
- Add the real public/private GitHub remotes and authentication. Push public first, replace the local public-flake URL with its actual remote, update/test/commit the lock, then push private. No remote URLs are assumed and nothing has been pushed.
- Before enrolling real clients, decide the stable Headscale URL/TLS, registration and access policy, DNS policy, and relay policy. The private HTTP URL is only for this lab.
- Cross-host addressing, an overlay/client rollout, migration and public ingress remain future decisions. No shared/distributed storage is introduced. Persistent runtime state currently exists on one disk; backups are not implemented.
## Nexus Console
The live cluster console is available at `http://192.168.178.192:8080/console/`.
See [CONSOLE.md](CONSOLE.md) for authentication, architecture, API, security boundaries and exact Fedora administration commands. The console is itself a declarative MicroVM with persistent runtime credentials and audit history.
{ lib, pkgs, ... }:
{
  imports = [
    ./hardware-configuration.nix
    ./storage.nix
  ];
  networking.hostName = "test-host";
  # Keep DHCP on the physical interface; networkd manages only the VM TAP.
  networking.useDHCP = lib.mkForce false;
  networking.interfaces.enp27s0.useDHCP = true;
  hardware.cpu.amd.updateMicrocode = true;
  boot.kernelModules = [ "kvm_amd" ];
  environment.systemPackages = [ pkgs.efibootmgr ];
  users.users.jonas = {
    isNormalUser = true;
    extraGroups = [ "wheel" ];
    openssh.authorizedKeys.keys = [
      "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHSGUjnGlQzkqu+HtOl4Rbs9kIzd4N9ghKIvCsSFp6tg jonas@fedora"
    ];
  };
  security.sudo.wheelNeedsPassword = true;
}
{ config, lib, pkgs, ... }:
{
  microvm.host.enable = true;
  # Fully declarative guests: mount each backing filesystem before creating
  # its share directories or starting the share daemon and guest.
  systemd.services = lib.mkMerge (lib.mapAttrsToList (name: vm:
    let
      sources = map (share: share.source)
        (lib.filter (share: share.source != "/nix/store") vm.config.config.microvm.shares);
    in lib.optionalAttrs (sources != [ ]) {
      "microvm@${name}".unitConfig.RequiresMountsFor = sources;
      "microvm-virtiofsd@${name}" = {
        unitConfig.RequiresMountsFor = sources;
        requires = [ "microvm-storage-${name}.service" ];
        after = [ "microvm-storage-${name}.service" ];
      };
      "microvm-storage-${name}" = {
        description = "Prepare mounted storage for MicroVM ${name}";
        unitConfig.RequiresMountsFor = sources;
        serviceConfig = {
          Type = "oneshot";
          RemainAfterExit = true;
          ExecStart = "${pkgs.systemd}/bin/systemd-tmpfiles --create "
            + lib.escapeShellArgs (map (source: "--prefix=${source}") sources);
        };
      };
    }
  ) (lib.filterAttrs (_: vm: vm.config != null) config.microvm.vms));
}
{
  description = "Private Nexus infrastructure deployment";
  inputs = {
    nixpkgs.url = "github:NixOS/nixpkgs/nixos-26.05";
    nexus-infra.url = "git+file:///etc/nixos/Nexus-Infra?ref=main";
    nexus-infra.inputs.nixpkgs.follows = "nixpkgs";
  };
  outputs = { nixpkgs, nexus-infra, ... }: {
    nixosConfigurations.test-host = nixpkgs.lib.nixosSystem {
      system = "x86_64-linux";
      specialArgs = { inherit nexus-infra; };
      modules = [
        nexus-infra.nixosModules.host-base
        nexus-infra.nixosModules.nexus-agent
        nexus-infra.nixosModules.microvm-host
        ./hosts/test-host/configuration.nix
        ./cluster/test-host.nix
      ];
    };
  };
}
